WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:08.000
REGINA HERZLINGER: So let&amp;#39;s get started with this framework.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.790
First step in the framework is a series of caveats.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:19.810
So caveat, that&amp;#39;s a fancy word for watch out.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:23.570
So what do you want to watch out for?

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:29.620
So I have a friend, very successful health care venture capitalist.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:37.370
And he said there&amp;#39;s a difference between literature, meaning a business

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:42.420
plan or an idea for a new venture, and life,

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:46.880
meaning the reality of that new venture.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:54.270
He said literature is all romance and no children.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.650
He didn&amp;#39;t use the word romance.

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:58.980
You know what word he used.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:04.849
But life, life, it&amp;#39;s all children and no romance.

00:01:04.849 --> 00:01:11.620
And he said that&amp;#39;s the way it is with health care innovation.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:17.120
The literature, the business plan, ha, it&amp;#39;s full of hearts and flowers.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.960
But the reality is very hard.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:25.390
So how do you know what&amp;#39;s literature, and how do you know what&amp;#39;s life?

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:32.210
Well, one thing you should be very careful of are true believers.

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:38.870
So true believers are the missionaries who have created this new venture.

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:41.320
And they deeply believe in it.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:45.470
They&amp;#39;re passionate about it, so passionate

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:50.860
that they may not see the world the way you would see the world.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:53.900
So don&amp;#39;t believe the true believers.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:55.640
I don&amp;#39;t mean they&amp;#39;re liars.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:56.710
Some people are.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:58.250
Most are not.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:03.210
What I mean is they see the world differently from the way

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:05.600
that you may see the world.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:10.280
So how do you get a reality check on the world?

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:13.360
You need to go back to basics.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:21.130
So if somebody says, the market for telemedicine is $30 billion,

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:22.650
what are you going to do with this?

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.950
Well, you have to understand the basics.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:29.760
How many people are going to be using telemedicine?

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:32.370
What will they be using it for?

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:35.330
Who is actually going to pay for this?

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:37.910
How much are they willing to pay?

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:42.540
And you&amp;#39;ve got to do this area by area of application

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.350
because the answers all differ.

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:50.110
So right away you know that innovating in health care,

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:52.876
it&amp;#39;s not all high-level stories.

00:02:52.876 --> 00:02:56.160
You got to get a lot of dirt under those fingernails

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:59.010
in order to do it appropriately.

